## Why purity matters for reconciliation

React assumes renders are **idempotent** — it may call your component multiple times (StrictMode, concurrent rendering). Side effects in render cause bugs that are hard to reproduce.

## Key takeaways

- Keep render logic pure: compute UI from props/state only.
- Side effects belong in `useEffect`, event handlers, or server actions.
- `React.memo` is the function-component equivalent of `PureComponent`.

Both hooks run **after** React commits DOM changes, but at different points relative to the browser paint.

## Timing comparison

| | `useLayoutEffect` | `useEffect` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| When | Synchronously after DOM mutation, **before paint** | Asynchronously **after paint** |
| Blocks paint? | Yes | No |
| Runs on server? | No (warns in SSR) | No |
| Typical use | DOM measurements, synchronous layout fixes | Data fetching, subscriptions, logging |

