## Does NOT trigger re-render

| Action | Why |
| --- | --- |
| `ref.current = value` | Refs are mutable boxes outside React's render cycle |
| Mutating state object in place | Same reference — React skips update |
| Parent re-render with same props + `React.memo` | Shallow prop compare passes |

```javascript
function Parent() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);
  return (
    <>
      <button onClick={() => setCount((c) => c + 1)}>{count}</button>
      <Child /> {/* re-renders every Parent click */}
    </>
  );
}

const Child = React.memo(() => <div>static</div>); // skips re-render
```

## Key insight

> Props don't cause re-renders — **parent re-renders** do. The child receives new props as a consequence.

## Key takeaways

- State/context changes and parent renders are the main triggers.
- `useRef` updates are invisible to React's scheduler.
- `React.memo` prevents parent-driven re-renders when props are shallowly equal.

`React.memo` wraps a component and **skips re-rendering** when props are shallowly equal to the previous render.

## Basic usage

```javascript
const ExpensiveList = React.memo(function ExpensiveList({ items, onSelect }) {
  return (
    <ul>
      {items.map((item) => (
        <li key={item} onClick={() => onSelect(item)}>{item}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  );
});
```

