## Fix 1: Split contexts by update frequency

```javascript
const ThemeContext = createContext('light');
const UserContext = createContext(null);
const CartContext = createContext([]);

// UserName only subscribes to UserContext
```

## Fix 2: Memoize the Provider value

```javascript
function AppProvider({ children }) {
  const [user, setUser] = useState(null);
  const [theme, setTheme] = useState('light');

  const value = useMemo(
    () => ({ user, theme, setUser, setTheme }),
    [user, theme]
  );

  return <AppContext.Provider value={value}>{children}</AppContext.Provider>;
}
```

Without `useMemo`, `value={{ user, theme }}` creates a new object every parent render → all consumers re-render.

## Fix 3: Split state and dispatch

```javascript
const StateContext = createContext(null);
const DispatchContext = createContext(null);

// Dispatch context value is stable (same dispatch function)
// Components that only call dispatch don't re-render on state changes
```

## Fix 4: External store with selectors

For high-frequency or granular updates, use **Zustand**, **Jotai**, or **Redux** with selectors instead of raw Context.

## Key takeaways

- Context is for low-frequency, cross-cutting data (theme, auth, locale).
- Never put rapidly changing values (scroll position, keystrokes) in Context.
- Split + memoize Provider values before reaching for external state libraries.

These are **rendering strategies** that decide where and when HTML is generated relative to the browser.

## Comparison

| Strategy | When rendered | Freshness | Best for |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **CSR** (Client-Side Rendering) | Browser after JS loads | Always client-fresh | Dashboards, authenticated apps |
| **SSR** (Server-Side Rendering) | Server on every request | Always fresh | Personalized, SEO-critical dynamic pages |
| **SSG** (Static Site Generation) | Build time | Stale until rebuild | Blogs, docs, marketing |
| **ISR** (Incremental Static Regeneration) | Build + background revalidate | Stale-while-revalidate | E-commerce, news with CDN scale |

